From b114fe5ec71b3137ef93721e307957125cf1011e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] iOS: Options dialog for small touch screens

On iOS the Options dialog works like the Settings app: a category list,
pages with a back button, and pages fitted to the phone width. The layout
code itself lives in the iOS app layer (app/ios/options_ios.cpp in the
opencpn-ios repository); options.cpp only gets the hooks that call it and
a few iOS-specific control settings.

All changes are inside #ifdef __OCPN__IOS__; other platforms are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
